CAT = "zare5Rep"; SEG = "REP"
Q = [
("Under the FAIS Act, a representative is a person who:",
 "Renders services for an FSP", ["Owns a product supplier", "Approves new FSP licences", "Supervises key individuals"],
 "A representative renders a financial service to a client for or on behalf of an FSP, under employment or another mandatory agreement."),
("A representative acts for the FSP under:",
 "A contract or mandate", ["Their own FSP licence", "The supplier's licence", "The Ombud's authority"],
 "A representative works under the FSP's licence, in terms of conditions of employment or another mandatory agreement."),
("Which person is NOT a representative under the FAIS Act?",
 "A clerk capturing forms", ["A call centre agent giving advice", "A broker submitting client claims", "A tied agent selling policies"],
 "People who give clerical, technical or administrative help in a subordinate capacity that needs no judgement and does not lead the client to a transaction are excluded."),
("Who accepts responsibility for a representative's actions within the mandate?",
 "The FSP", ["Only the representative", "The product supplier", "The Ombud for FSPs"],
 "An FSP that appoints a representative must accept responsibility for the representative's activities performed within the scope of the mandate."),
("Before rendering services for an FSP, a representative must be able to show:",
 "Proof of the FSP's mandate", ["Their own Ombud registration", "A personal bank guarantee", "A letter from each client"],
 "The Act requires a representative to be able to provide confirmation, certified by the FSP, that a service contract or other mandate exists and that the FSP accepts responsibility."),
("The fit and proper requirements for a representative include:",
 "Honesty and good standing", ["A minimum age of 25 years", "Owning their own office", "Five years with one FSP"],
 "Fit and proper requirements cover honesty, integrity and good standing, competence and continuous professional development, and for FSPs operational ability and financial soundness."),
("Which of these is part of a representative's competence requirements?",
 "Passing the regulatory exam", ["Holding a credit card", "Owning shares in the FSP", "Meeting a monthly sales figure"],
 "Competence is made up of experience, qualifications, the regulatory examination, class of business and product specific training, and CPD."),
("When must a representative complete class of business training?",
 "Before serving clients in that class", ["Within five years of appointment", "Only for Category II business", "Only after passing the RE5"],
 "Section 29(1) of BN 194 of 2017 requires class of business training to be completed before rendering any financial service on a financial product in that class."),
("For a representative of a Category I FSP, product specific training must be completed:",
 "Before dealing in the product", ["Only for investment products", "Once every ten years", "Only if the client asks"],
 "Section 29(1) of BN 194 of 2017 requires product specific training before rendering a financial service on the product. Section 28(3) exempts Category II, IIA and III FSPs and their representatives."),
("Which regulatory examination must a representative pass, whatever the FSP's licence category?",
 "RE 5", ["RE 1", "RE 3", "RE 4"],
 "Table A of BN 194 of 2017 lists RE 5 for representatives in every category. RE 1 is for FSPs and key individuals, with RE 3 or RE 4 added for some categories."),
("Continuous professional development (CPD) for representatives means:",
 "Learning in each CPD cycle", ["A one-off induction course", "The regulatory exam itself", "Reading the FSP's newsletter"],
 "Representatives must complete a minimum number of CPD hours in each 12-month CPD cycle (6, 12 or 18 hours under BN 194, depending on the classes of business) to keep their knowledge current."),
("Under BN 194 of 2017, each CPD cycle runs from:",
 "1 June to 31 May", ["1 January to 31 December", "1 March to 28 February", "1 April to 31 March"],
 "BN 194 defines the CPD cycle as 12 months starting on 1 June each year and ending on 31 May the next year."),
("Which would most likely mean a person does not meet the honesty and integrity requirements?",
 "A conviction for fraud", ["A speeding fine", "A lapsed gym contract", "A change of employer last year"],
 "Dishonesty offences such as fraud or theft count against honesty, integrity and good standing. Minor matters unrelated to honesty do not."),
("A representative is charged with theft. The representative should:",
 "Tell the FSP at once", ["Wait for the verdict", "Tell only their clients", "Move to another FSP quickly"],
 "The FSP must know of matters affecting a representative's honesty and integrity, so it can assess whether the person still meets the fit and proper requirements."),
("A representative processes a client's instruction to switch funds without recommending anything. This is:",
 "An intermediary service", ["Advice to the client", "No financial service", "A discretionary service"],
 "Carrying out a client's instruction on a product, with no recommendation, is an intermediary service rather than advice."),
("A representative tells a client, \"This policy is the best fit for your needs.\" This is:",
 "Advice", ["An intermediary service only", "Factual information", "Not a financial service"],
 "A recommendation about which product to buy is advice, and the full advice process and record of advice apply."),
("Which of these is excluded from the definition of advice?",
 "Answers to admin queries", ["A proposal to switch funds", "Guidance on which policy to buy", "A suggestion to cancel cover"],
 "Answers to routine administrative queries are excluded from advice, along with factual information on procedure and objective product information."),
("A representative may render services under supervision when they:",
 "Lack the experience needed", ["Have been debarred", "Have a fraud conviction", "Have no mandate from any FSP"],
 "The exemption for services under supervision (FAIS Notice 86 of 2018) lets a representative who does not yet meet experience or qualification requirements work under a qualified supervisor. Honesty failures are not cured by supervision."),
("The supervisor of a representative must:",
 "Meet the competence rules", ["Be the FSP's compliance officer", "Work for the product supplier", "Be a practising attorney too"],
 "A supervisor must meet the experience, qualification and regulatory exam requirements for the relevant category and product."),
("Under supervision, who oversees the supervisee's advice?",
 "The appointed supervisor", ["The client being advised", "The Ombud for FSPs", "The product supplier"],
 "The supervisor oversees, reviews and signs off the supervised representative's services as the supervision arrangements require."),
("Supervision of a representative may end when the representative:",
 "Meets the competence rules", ["Has served one month", "Has 50 clients on record", "Passes a credit check"],
 "Supervision is for representatives who do not yet meet the competence requirements; once they do, they may render services unsupervised."),
("Why must the FSP keep a register of its representatives?",
 "To show who acts for it", ["To track their holidays", "To rank their monthly sales", "To set their commission"],
 "The register records who is appointed to render services for the FSP and in which categories, and the Authority keeps a central register from it."),
("A representative leaves the FSP. The FSP must:",
 "Remove them from the register", ["Keep them listed for a year", "Hand them its client records", "Notify the Ombud for FSPs"],
 "The FSP must keep its register current and remove representatives who no longer act for it, updating the Authority's central register."),
("The Authority's central register of representatives lets the public:",
 "Check a person's status", ["See each rep's commission", "Book an appointment", "Lodge a complaint"],
 "Clients can check on the central register whether a person is appointed as a representative, and for which FSP."),
("A representative must render financial services in line with:",
 "The General Code of Conduct", ["The supplier's sales scripts", "The client's wishes alone", "Their own judgement alone"],
 "The General Code of Conduct and any specific code for the product apply to every representative's services."),
("Which act would be outside a representative's role?",
 "Advising outside the licence", ["Submitting a claim for a client", "Explaining policy exclusions", "Doing a needs analysis"],
 "A representative may act only within the FSP's licence categories and the mandate. The other three are normal parts of the role."),
("A 'recognised qualification' for a representative is one that:",
 "The Authority recognises", ["Comes from any field of study", "Takes any course over a week", "A product supplier awards"],
 "Qualifications must appear on the Authority's list of recognised qualifications for the relevant class of business."),
("Under the fit and proper requirements, 'experience' means:",
 "Relevant hands-on work", ["Any work in an office", "Time spent studying", "Years as a client of an FSP"],
 "Experience is practical, appropriate experience in rendering financial services in the relevant class of business and products."),
]
